@startuml diagram
title Sandbox cleanup and Mate tool manager migration

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Observed baseline" {
  [Agent tools] as old_tools
  [Hybrid tools] as hybrid
  [ExecutionRouter] as router
  [Local JVM tools] as old_local
  [DockerSandboxClient] as docker
  [DinD sidecar] as dind

  old_tools --> hybrid : tool schema
  hybrid --> router : LOCAL or SANDBOX
  router --> old_local : local path
  router --> docker : sandbox path
  docker --> dind : DOCKER_HOST
}

package "Target runtime" {
  [AgentSession] as session
  [ToolCatalog] as catalog
  [Local base tools] as local
  [ListMateTool] as list_mate
  [CallMateTool] as call_mate
  [MateToolClient] as client
  [MateService tool manager] as mate

  session --> catalog : select local tools
  catalog --> local : executable AgentTool
  session --> list_mate : metadata query
  session --> call_mate : managed tool call
  list_mate --> client
  call_mate --> client
  client --> mate : query and invoke
}

note right of router
Observed behavior:
tool.execution selects local or Docker execution.
Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/execution/ExecutionRouter.java
end note

note right of catalog
Design reason:
one local catalog plus MateService authority
removes duplicate execution routing and DinD.
Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/catalog/
end note

note bottom of session
Java divergence: Agent Core ToolExecutionMode remains for sequential or parallel tool calls.
It is unrelated to the deleted local sandbox execution mode.
end note
@enduml
